## 7. Sensor Architecture

### HC-SR04

Used for detecting obstacles in front of the robot.

```text
HC-SR04
   ↓
ESP32
   ↓
Distance
   ↓
Obstacle Detection
```

### DHT22

Used to measure:

* Temperature
* Humidity

```text
DHT22
  ↓
ESP32
  ↓
Temperature / Humidity
```

---

## 8. OLED Display

The SSD1306 OLED is connected to the ESP32 using **I²C**.

It can display information such as:

```text
SYSTEM AWAKE
LISTENING...
MOVING
OBSTACLE DETECTED
FAN ON
LIGHT ON
```

It can also be used for VORTEX's expressive eye/interface animations.

---

## 9. Audio System

The DFPlayer Mini is connected to the ESP32.

```text
ESP32
  ↓
DFPlayer Mini
  ↓
Speaker
```

Example:

```text
System Start
     ↓
"Hi Buddy, How can I help you?"
```

Audio can also provide feedback for commands and system events.

---

## 10. Communication

VORTEX 2.0 uses different communication methods:

| Communication | Used For         |
| ------------- | ---------------- |
| UART          | VC-02 ↔ ESP32    |
| UART          | ESP32 ↔ DFPlayer |
| I²C           | ESP32 ↔ OLED     |
| GPIO          | Sensors & Motors |
| Wi-Fi         | ESP32 ↔ Blynk    |
| Wi-Fi         | ESP8266 ↔ Blynk  |

